 resignation 43%, mate 35%, clock 21% (median move 26)."],"plan":"Usually continues exf5 (30%), Nxe5 (28%), d3 (14%). Your bishop is the one to watch (often landing on d7, b4). Aim at their bishop.","tips":["Aim for a steady edge by move 12: 64% of games get there, and 47% reach +6 by move 21.","Watch your bishop: it is behind 21% of your lost leads, 1.3\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the light-squared bishop (65%), landing on d7, b4, d6.","Aim at their bishop: it is behind 22% of their lost leads, 1.4\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the dark-squared bishop (51%). The reply wins it outright 27% of the time. Take it with a queen.","Material changes hands for you on e4 and f3: build pressure there.","They win material on h8 and f5: keep those squares defended.","Look for the discovered check: it appears 3.1\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Latvian Gambit","children":[]}